[manifest]
desc="Out-of-tree driver for IT87/IT86 hardware monitoring chips (target_commit_sha)<br>Prebuilt modules support the following kernel versions<br>6.12.18-trim#3, 6.18.6-trim#297, 6.18.18-trim#427, 6.18.18-trim#570, 6.18.18-trim#587, 6.18.18-trim#717<br>6.18.18.c788-trim#788, 6.18.18.c877-trim#877, 6.18.18.c938-trim#938, 6.18.18.c952-trim#952, 6.18.18.c1032-trim#1032, 6.18.18.c1078-trim#1078, 6.18.18.c1126-trim#1126, 6.18.18.c1168-trim#1168<br>When no prebuilt module is available for the current kernel, an optional local build in chroot can be used as a fallback. This carries additional risk; waiting for a supported prebuilt release is recommended.<br>This driver package is provided and maintained by community members.<br>For support, contact community members or open an issue in this repository and include exported logs."
changelog="Updated the driver to target_commit_sha with support for the currently adapted kernels."

[wizard]
install_step_title="Kernel module installation"
install_mode_label="Choose an installation method"
prebuilt_only_label="Use prebuilt modules only (recommended)"
allow_local_build_label="Allow a local build when missing (high risk)"
local_build_warning="<strong>Warning: We strongly recommend using prebuilt modules only and waiting for a release that supports your kernel.</strong><br><br>Local builds are intended only for advanced users who can diagnose and accept kernel-driver risks. Compilation may saturate CPU, memory, and disk I/O for an extended period, causing severe slowdowns, interrupted services, or an unresponsive system.<br><br>The resulting module has not been pre-validated and may fail to load or destabilize the system, potentially requiring a restart."

